{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.FreeAlgebra","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Operations","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.RingQuot","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Defs"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.hom_ext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.hom_ext","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Quotient.lean#L216-L240","doc":"**Uniqueness half of the universal property.** Two `R`-algebra maps out of\n`IwahoriHeckeQuot R q S` that agree on every generator `T s` are equal.\n\nTogether with `universal_property_hecke_quadratic` (existence) this gives the full\n`∃!` statement. It was previously recorded as an `axiom` in `Defn.lean`, on the\nstated ground that the container had no `lake` binary and `elan` could not reach the\nLean release server; that obstacle is gone, and the proof is three steps:\n\n`RingQuot.mkAlgHom` is surjective, so it suffices that the two composites with it\nagree. Those are algebra maps out of a *free* algebra, so `FreeAlgebra.hom_ext`\nreduces the question to agreement on the generators `ι s` — which is the hypothesis,\nsince `T s` is by definition `mkAlgHom (ι s)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.universal_property_hecke_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.universal_property_hecke_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Quotient.lean#L197-L214","doc":"**Universal property of the Hecke quotient (Hecke-quadratic\nfragment).** Any `R`-algebra map from `FreeAlgebra R S` that\nsends each `heckeQuadraticRelation` to `0` factors through\n`IwahoriHeckeQuot R q S` via `RingQuot.liftAlgHom`.  (The target `A`\nmay be any `R`-algebra — not necessarily commutative.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.T_hecke_quadratic_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.T_hecke_quadratic_relation","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Quotient.lean#L183-L195","doc":"**The Hecke quadratic relation holds in the quotient.**\nThe generator `T_s` satisfies `(T_s - q)(T_s + 1) = 0` in\n`IwahoriHeckeQuot R q S`, because `mkAlgHom` identifies the quadratic\ngenerator with `0` (it is `heckeRel`-related to `0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.T","kind":"def","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Quotient.lean#L178-L181","doc":"**The image of a generator** `T_s ∈ IwahoriHeckeQuot R q S`\nunder the quotient algebra map `RingQuot.mkAlgHom`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.instAlgebraIwahoriHeckeQuot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.instAlgebraIwahoriHeckeQuot","kind":"instance","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Quotient.lean#L175-L176","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.instRingIwahoriHeckeQuot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.instRingIwahoriHeckeQuot","kind":"instance","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Quotient.lean#L165-L173","doc":"`IwahoriHeckeQuot R q S` carries the canonical (non-commutative) ring and\n`R`-algebra structure inherited from `RingQuot`.  Note: this algebra is\n**not** commutative (the free algebra `FreeAlgebra R S` is not, and the\nHecke quadratic relation does not impose commutativity), so there is no\n`CommRing` instance — that was the bug in the previous `Ideal.Quotient`\nconstruction, which only applies to two-sided ideals of commutative\nrings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.IwahoriHeckeQuot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.IwahoriHeckeQuot","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Quotient.lean#L152-L163","doc":"**The (partial) Iwahori-Hecke algebra** — the `RingQuot` of the free\nalgebra by the Hecke quadratic relations.\n\nSprint 2 deliverable: type + (non-commutative) ring + `R`-algebra\nstructure are sorry-free via Mathlib's `RingQuot`. The full Iwahori-Hecke\nadditionally quotients by braid relations; that step is Sprint 2 follow-up.\n\nNaming: `IwahoriHeckeQuot` distinguishes from the Sprint 1\n`IwahoriHecke` opaque stub; once Sprint 2 follow-up establishes\nthe equivalence, the two unify. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.heckeRel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.heckeRel","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Quotient.lean#L143-L150","doc":"**The Hecke quotient relation**: each quadratic generator is related to\n`0`.  Because `FreeAlgebra R S` is **non-commutative**, the Hecke algebra\nis built as the algebra-by-relations quotient `RingQuot (heckeRel)`\n(Mathlib's tool for quotienting a non-commutative algebra by a relation),\nnot as an `Ideal.Quotient` (which gives a commutative quotient of a\ncommutative ring — the wrong construction here). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.heckeIdeal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.heckeIdeal","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Quotient.lean#L131-L141","doc":"**The Hecke ideal** — two-sided ideal of `FreeAlgebra R S`\ngenerated by the Hecke quadratic relations.\n\nSprint 2 scope: we include only the Hecke quadratic relations\nhere. The braid relations require the Coxeter order function\n`m : S → S → ℕ` which is in flux in Mathlib's `CoxeterSystem`\nAPI; they are added in the Sprint 2 follow-up once the order\naccessor stabilises. The quadratic-only ideal is still a\nwell-defined sub-algebra of the full Iwahori-Hecke. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.heckeQuadraticGenerators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.heckeQuadraticGenerators","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Quotient.lean#L126-L129","doc":"The **set** of Hecke quadratic relations, indexed by simple\nreflections. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.heckeQuadraticRelation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient.heckeQuadraticRelation","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Quotient.lean#L119-L124","doc":"**Hecke quadratic generator**: the polynomial\n`(T_s - q) * (T_s + 1)` in the free algebra, for a simple\nreflection `s ∈ S`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}